<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39182" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδηλ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seen clearly,
			manifest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				442
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εἶναί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.97
				</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιεῖν τισί, ἤν . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					38
				</span></i>
			: c. part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐστι
				κλέπτων</span> is <i>detected</i> stealing, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				661
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. μάλιστα γίνεται [ἄνθρωπος] ἀπὸ</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑπταετέος μεχρι τεσσαρεσκαιδεκαετέος</span>
			<i>formed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Carn.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>.
				<i>indicative</i> of a crisis to come, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				2.24
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(2).510
			</span></i>: so in neut. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῆς ἀρετῆς ἐπίδηλα</span>”
				<i>as a witness of . . ,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					IG
					12(7).286
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. <i>distinguished, remarkable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				21.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>.
			<i>like</i>, <i>resembling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					368
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Acut.</u>
					45
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cael.</u>
				297b34
			</span></i>, etc.: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>GA</u>
					728b29
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-οτέρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HA</u>
					604a2
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότατα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				510a5
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-οτάτως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>GA</u>
					727a23
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίζηλος</span>.)</div>
